tion\" data-id=\"9775265\"><a href=\"/opinion/2449391/singleton-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Singleton v. State\">623 S. W. 2d 180</a></span>; No. 81-6353, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1302254\"><a href=\"/opinion/1302254/bassett-v-commonwealth/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Bassett v. Commonwealth\">222 Va. 844</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1302254\"><a href=\"/opinion/1302254/bassett-v-commonwealth/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Bassett v. Commonwealth\">284 S. E. 2d 844</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9031996,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":597,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b982-10\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AKHq\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b982-11\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}